    "text": "Builder: implement the adopted MCP-core runtime as its own follow-up after declared-acts stage 5's MCP work is committed; final integration follows reviewed stage 5 on main. Compose planner's contract handoff b22b6dcebcaad254b462ca9b35dbd9b863163789 with the delivered generic surfaces. This runtime is not needed by the recorded first jam development task and is not an added jam-readiness gate. Preserve all a9788a59/775acdd3 core features and stage-5 behavior. Every required edit in docs/protocol.md section 34.2 at that exact head is in scope.",
    "body": {
      "conditions": "(1) Complete R-API-9/13/14/15 and all section-34.2 edits at the named contract head: fourteen named tools plus act/acts; lanes/lane/proposal/operation use RoomApi reads, with structured unknown-ID results. (2) Advertise titles, conforming success/refusal output schemas, fixed annotations, descriptions \u003c=1000 characters and instructions \u003c=512. Generic act hints are conservative and fixed; acts is read-only. (3) Implement builder/reviewer/observer/all toolsets, authorization defaults/filtering, the toolset query and bad-request for unknown names. Listing is deterministic and independent of earlier calls; unlisted calls still face Room admission. acts is in all sets; act is in builder/reviewer/all subject to authority; observer has no mutating tool. Cover checker roster role without granting review/claim authority. Never expand grant maps or silently rebind intent. (4) Require idempotencyKey in schemas/runtime for every act tool, including act. Test missing-key refusal and lost-result retries with one effect and original results; preserve existing revocation/receipt rules. Update generated AGENTS.md retry guidance. (5) Validate finite integer waitMs from 0 through 45000 on attention/workspace/land/operation; preserve defaults, caller-specific attention waits, operation until/default terminal states and fresh current state on timeout. Waiting holds no lease, slot or Room state. (6) Preserve all stage-5 binding/history, custody, v1 controls and fa120186 v2 generic-check guards/tests; automated stage-4 check-service jobs remain separate. (7) Reconcile main, all four planner contract paths, section 34/amendment 7 and stage-5 section-33 changes. Planner retains a9788a59/ee3d9036 scope and republishes its artifacts at the final head. Report all changed-path artifacts and one exact composed head; independent review binds every scope it closes. Meaningful interface/integration tests and named red mutations for new guards; relevant root/MCP/client/CLI gates pass at that head. Neither the contract draft nor stage 5 alone closes this runtime request.",
